+// gs_gpu_backend.inl - opt-in OpenGL 3.3 GS renderer (PS2X_GS_GPU=1), stage one.
+//
+// Included at the end of gs_frontend.cpp (instead of being its own translation unit) so
+// that enabling it needs no CMake change / reconfigure. It is only instantiated when the
+// env var PS2X_GS_GPU=1 is set; the CPU rasterizer stays the default and the fallback.
+//
+// Design:
+//  * All GL work runs on one dedicated thread with an offscreen (surfaceless) EGL
+//    context. libEGL is dlopen'ed and every GL entry point comes from eglGetProcAddress,
+//    so nothing new is linked.
+//  * The public GSRasterBackend methods enqueue commands in order; methods whose result
+//    is observable (Present, ReadVram, Snapshot, ClearFramebuffer, local->host) wait.
+//  * An internal GSCpuBackend on the same VRAM handles transfers, CLUT loads, texture
+//    decode, Present (display conversion) and local->host readback.
+//  * Render targets: one 1024x1024 RGBA16F texture per FRAME.fbp (alpha stored as A/128
+//    so DST_ALPHA / FIX / As can be used as GS blend factors). Depth: DEPTH32F per ZBUF.zbp,
+//    storing z / 2^32 (clamped to the Z format max).
+//  * Coherency: targets are uploaded from VRAM when created or stale, and resolved
+//    GPU->VRAM (glReadPixels + swizzled write) before anything reads that memory on the
+//    CPU side: Present, ReadVram/Snapshot, transfers touching it, textures/CLUTs read from
+//    it (render-to-texture), local->local copies. CPU writes mark overlapping targets stale.
+//  * PS2X_GS_SCALE=N (1..4, default 1): internal resolution. Colour targets, depth and the
+//    destination-copy scratch are N*kDim square; draws use an N-times viewport/scissor (vertex
+//    positions stay in GS pixels, so nothing else changes). Resolves to VRAM downsample through
+//    a native-size texture (linear 2x2 average; PS2X_GS_SCALE_RESOLVE=nearest picks one sample),
+//    uploads from VRAM are drawn back up with nearest. Present reads the displayed rectangle
+//    straight from the scaled target when it is current (single CRT, no preferred source);
+//    anything else (FMVs uploaded by transfers, merge circuit, ...) falls back to the native
+//    CPU conversion. Render-to-texture effects sample the native resolve (as on hardware).
+//  * Textures are decoded on the CPU (GSCpuBackend::DecodeTextureRgba) into RGBA8 GL
+//    textures cached by TEX0/TEXA/CLUT hash and validated by per-8KB-page generations.
+
